Package: tim
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends},
         ${misc:Depends},
         adduser
Description: Terminal Instant Messenger (TIM) server
 TIM is an SSH-accessible instant messaging server. Clients connect over
 SSH and get a Tcl-scriptable terminal prompt to read and post messages;
 fan-out between sessions is done through an external MQTT broker, and
 messages are persisted in SQLite.
 .
 The package installs a systemd unit running TIM under a dedicated
 unprivileged system user. State lives in /var/lib/tim/; configuration
 in /etc/tim/config.json.
